WEBVTT

00:07:28.574 --> 00:07:31.374
and surrounded by water?

00:07:31.374 --> 00:07:32.976
How were we going to find housing

00:07:32.976 --> 00:07:35.274
for that many new New Yorkers?

00:07:35.274 --> 00:07:37.087
And if we couldn't spread out,

00:07:37.087 --> 00:07:38.901
which was probably a good thing,

00:07:38.901 --> 00:07:41.720
where could new housing go?

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:43.353
And what about cars?

00:07:43.353 --> 00:07:47.465
Our city couldn't possibly handle any more cars.

00:07:47.465 --> 00:07:50.299
So what were we going to do?

00:07:50.299 --> 00:07:54.276
If we couldn't spread out, we had to go up.

00:07:54.276 --> 00:07:55.310
And if we had to go up,

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:57.092
we had to go up in places

00:07:57.092 --> 00:07:59.101
where you wouldn't need to own a car.

00:07:59.101 --> 00:08:01.964
So that meant using one of our greatest assets: